  "notes": "Cash-basis village. Governmental lines from the p4 Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (Total column); the statement rolls forward fund balance, so beginning/ending go to *_fund_balance; cash fields left null as in FY2024 (cash lines are on the p3 balance sheet). Aligned with FY2024 (2026-11-12): business_type measure cash (cash + CDs), Taxes: Other kept as other (p2 Homestead/other is a mixed label). Interest income is printed under other financing sources, below Total Receipts (outside_printed_total). Charges for services 2,365.76 is omitted on p4 but included in its total; taken from the p10 comparative governmental statement. Business-type from the p6 proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenditures and Changes in Net Position (Total column), measure net position (cash-basis net position incl. certificates of deposit); no single printed total, so receipts = operating revenues + interest and disbursements = operating expenses + debt service. The only supplementary schedule is the all-funds budget statement p9 (combined), so per the per-fund rule detail is one line per fund column of the p4 and p6 statements; Keno fund column has no activity. p10/p11 are comparative copies of the statements (p11 differs from p6, see report_discrepancies). Balance sheet: governmental lines from the p3 governmental funds statement (totals equal the government-wide governmental column p1), business-type lines from the p1 Proprietary column. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
}
